{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 13940514470384553950, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {".pytest_cache/.gitignore": {"bytes": 37, "mtime": 1791871802.910502, "sha256": "3ed731b65d06150c138e2dadb0be0697550888a6b47eb8c45ecc9adba8b8e9bd"}, ".pytest_cache/CACHEDIR.TAG": {"bytes": 191, "mtime": 1791871802.910502, "sha256": "37dc88ef9a0abeddbe81053a6dd8fdfb13afb613045ea1eb4a5c815a74a3bde4"}, ".pytest_cache/README.md": {"bytes": 302, "mtime": 1791871802.910502, "sha256": "73fd6fccdd802c419a6b2d983d6c3173b7da97558ac4b589edec2dfe443db9ad"}, ".pytest_cache/v/cache/nodeids": {"bytes": 585, "mtime": 1791871802.910502, "sha256": "7949f1920246a44e36c0839fd5b8ba7e201974e5e3b3e4732e7f98932168b6a3"}, "pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 634, "mtime": 1791871767.607082, "sha256": "a544391f6d9a1b667daa64770ba14ab70336fe58a787ed8afad7999bbaa7590f"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 537, "mtime": 1791871771.3794327, "sha256": "215bb4cb580c796a04e853cf4a39509c0305c1c7c8d344886a0a2313f3348ac0"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/10/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 3, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/10/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`repr()` breaks on `Decimal` inputs (it returns `\"Decimal('1.5')\"`). `str()` gives the same shortest form for floats and also handles ints and Decimals, so I'll switch to it.\nAdding a regression test, then running everything.\nFixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`. All 9 tests pass, the 8 new cases plus the existing `test_split`. I ran them with `uv run --with pytest` because pytest isn't installed for the system `python3`.\n\n**Why it happened:** there were two separate causes in `pricing/money.py`:\n1. **Float storage:** `2.675` can't be stored exactly; Python holds it as `2.67499999999999982\u2026`, so `round(x, 2)` correctly rounds it down. `1.005` has the same problem.\n2. **Tie-breaking:** on an exact tie, Python's `round()` goes to the nearest even digit (`round(0.125, 2) == 0.12`), not half up as the docstring says.\n\n**What changed:** `round_money` now converts the number to its shortest decimal text (`str(2.675)` is `\"2.675\"`, the value the customer sees) and rounds that up to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. It also accepts ints and `Decimal` values. Negative ties round away from zero (`-2.675` gives `-2.68`). `add_vat` gets the fix automatically because it calls `round_money`.\n\n**Test added:** `tests/test_round_money.py` covers `2.675`, `1.005`, the exact ties `0.125` and `0.135`, a value that should round down, ints and a negative value.\n\n**One limit:** the fix rounds the float exactly as Python prints it. If an earlier calculation already put the value slightly off a tie (for example `x * 1.2` inside `add_vat` coming out as `2.67499999999999`), it will still round down. The real fix for that is to keep amounts as `Decimal` or as whole cents from start to finish, which is a bigger change I didn't make.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 10, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 277727, "requests_cache_write": 13115, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1782884, "requests_count": 10, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 2854, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial10", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 18, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T06:09:08.038470+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 62.988, "t_checker_s": 0.486, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-bugfix-regress", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2876, "tokens_cache_read": 277727, "tokens_cache_write": 13115, "tokens_fresh": 2876, "tokens_input_uncached": 22, "tokens_main_cache_read": 277727, "tokens_main_cache_write": 13115, "tokens_main_calls": 10, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 22, "tokens_main_output": 2854, "tokens_output": 2854, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 277727, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 13115, "tokens_proxy_calls": 10, "tokens_proxy_input